  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>

        <exercise id="_6a5dfa57-fef9-41e5-b8cd-c8e299fa4c13" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">Here is an inequality: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>Select two of the values that
              are a solution to the inequality.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00003">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00004">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.1.</para>
            <para id="para-00005">The correct answers are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00006">Substitute the number 1 in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to see how much it would cost to rent a
              scooter for 1 hour. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> To rent a scooter for 1 hour, it costs $20 from Company A and $15 from Company B.
              Company A costs more than Company B. To rent a scooter for 1 hour, it costs $20 from
              Company A and $15 from Company B. Company A costs more than Company B.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c160b1e0-fda6-40eb-a8da-4e31848f0df5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Which number line is represented by the inequality <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>≤</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00008"> 
                <media alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 6. The number line to the right of 6 is highlighted.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00009"> 
                <media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 6. The number line to the left of 6 is highlighted.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00010">  
                <media alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 6. The number line to the left of 6 is highlighted.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_03.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00011">  
                <media alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 6. The number line to the right of 6 is highlighted. ">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_04.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00012">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00013">A.</para>
            <para id="para-00014">B.</para>
            <para id="para-00015">C.</para>
            <para id="para-00016">D.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00017">Correct! 
                <media alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 6. The number line to the left of 6 is highlighted.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_05.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00018">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.2</para>
            <para id="para-00019">The correct answer is 
                <media alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 6. The number line to the left of 6 is highlighted.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_06.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00020"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> means that the solution would be any number less than or equal to 6.
              The graph would have a filled in circle on the number 6, because it can be equal to 6.
              The arrow would point to infinity on the left of the 6, because it is less than 6. The
              graph would have a filled in circle on the number 6, because it can be equal to 6. The
              arrow would point to infinity on the left of the 6, because it is less than 6.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <para id="para-00021">For questions 3 – 4, use the following information:</para>
      <para id="para-00022">
        <quote id="quote-00001">Scooter rental company A charges $9 per hour plus a $11 initiation fee. Scooter
        rental company B charges $15 per hour.</quote>
     </para>

        <exercise id="eadc8e80-78e7-4b3a-bf8a-ae7a81f3a6b4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00023">A customer writes the following inequality to represent the situation: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00024">Which of the following is true about the given inequality?</para>
            <para id="para-00025">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00026">Company A costs more than Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00027">Company A costs less than Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00028">Company A costs the same as Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00029">h represents the number of scooters rented.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00030">Correct! Company A costs more than Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00031">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00032">The correct answer is Company A costs more than Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00033">Substitute the number 1 in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to see how much it would cost to rent a
              scooter for 1 hour. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> To rent a scooter for 1 hour, it costs $20 from Company A and $15 from Company B.
              Company A costs more than Company B. To rent a scooter for 1 hour, it costs $20 from
              Company A and $15 from Company B. Company A costs more than Company B.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_7c8cc139-3f1c-48ef-aa50-44fc5400af42" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00034">For which number of hours does Company B cost less?</para>
            <para id="para-00035">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00036">1 hour</para>
            <para id="para-00037">2 hours</para>
            <para id="para-00038">3 hours</para>
            <para id="para-00039">4 hours</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00040">Correct! 1 hour</para>
            <para id="para-00041">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.3</para>
            <para id="para-00042">The correct answer is 1 hour.</para>
            <para id="para-00043"> Substitute the number 1 in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to see how much it would cost to rent a
              scooter for 1 hour. Company A: 9(1)+11=$20 Company A: 9(1)+11=$20 Company B: 15(1)=$15
              Company B: 15(1)=$15 To rent a scooter for 1 hour, it costs $20 from Company A and $15
              from Company B. To rent a scooter for 1 hour, it costs $20 from Company A and $15 from
              Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00044"> Substitute the number 2 in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to see how much it would cost to rent a
              scooter for 2 hours. Company A: Company A: 9(2)+11=$29 9(2)+11=$29 Company B:
              15(2)=$30 Company B: 15(2)=$30 To rent a scooter for 2 hours, it costs $29 from
              Company A and $30 from Company B. To rent a scooter for 2 hours, it costs $29 from
              Company A and $30 from Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00045"> Substitute the number 3 in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to see how much it would cost to rent a
              scooter for 3 hours. Company A: 9(3)+11=$38 Company A: 9(3)+11=$38 Company B:
              15(3)=$45 Company B: 15(3)=$45 To rent a scooter for 3 hours, it costs $38 from
              Company A and $45 from Company B. To rent a scooter for 3 hours, it costs $38 from
              Company A and $45 from Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00046"> Substitute the number 4 in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to see how much it would cost to rent a
              scooter for 4 hours. Company A: 9(4)+11=$47 Company A: 9(4)+11=$47 Company B:
              15(4)=$60 Company B: 15(4)=$60 To rent a scooter for 4 hours, it costs $47 from
              Company A and $60 from Company B. To rent a scooter for 4 hours, it costs $47 from
              Company A and $60 from Company B.</para>
            <para id="para-00047">Company B costs the least for 1 hour.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <para id="para-00048">For questions 5 – 7, use the following information:</para>
        <para id="para-00049">
          <quote id="quote-00002">Cycle Rentals offers 20 membership points for each day that a customer rents a
          bike. Bikes Unlimited offers 5 membership points for each day that a customer rents a
          bike plus 60 points for joining the membership club.</quote>
       </para>
        <exercise id="_41abc371-b9ff-4743-8f77-ac06b17d1353" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00050">The equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> represents a possible constraint about the
              situation. Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00051"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> = ____</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00052">Correct! The correct answer is 4. If you rent a bike for longer than 4 days, you
              earn more membership points at Cycle Rentals.</para>
            <para id="para-00053"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00054">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00055">The correct answer is 4. If you rent a bike for longer than 4 days, you earn more
              membership points at Cycle Rentals.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="bc34b533-547f-47a7-942e-01f28d487514" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00056">Which shop offers more membership points if you rent a bike for longer than the
              constraint you found in the previous question?</para>
            <para id="para-00057">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00058">Cycle Rentals</para>
            <para id="para-00059">Bikes Unlimited</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00060">Correct! Cycle Rentals</para>
            <para id="para-00061">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00062">The correct answer is Cycle Rentals.</para>
            <para id="para-00063"> The constraint from question 5 is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Since a number larger than 4 is needed
              to determine which shop offers more membership points if you rent a bike for longer
              than the constraint, choose to substitute in the number 5 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to calculate how
              many membership points can be earned in 5 days. Since a number larger than 4 is needed
              to determine which shop offers more membership points if you rent a bike for longer
              than the constraint, choose to substitute in the number 5 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> to calculate how
              many membership points can be earned in 5 days. Cycle Rentals: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
              membership points Cycle Rentals: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> membership points Bikes Unlimited:
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>85</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> membership points Bikes Unlimited:
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>85</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> membership points</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_90b0f163-6e68-4323-abe1-441b5d71512c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00064">Which number line represents the solution to the inequality, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>,
              representing the situation when you earn more membership points at Cycle Rentals?</para>
            <para id="para-00065">
              
                <media alt="A number line is shown from 2 to 6 with an open circle on the point 4. The number line to the right of 4 is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_07.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00066">
              
                <media alt="A number line is shown from 2 to 6 with a closed circle on the point 4. The number line to the right of 4 is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_08.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00067">
              
                <media alt="A number line is shown from 2 to 6 with a closed circle on the point 4. The number line to the left of 4 is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_09.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00068">
              
                <media alt="A number line is shown from 2 to 6 with an open circle on the point 4. The number line to the left of 4 is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_10.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00069">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00070">A.</para>
            <para id="para-00071">B.</para>
            <para id="para-00072">C.</para>
            <para id="para-00073">D.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00074">Correct! 
                <media alt="A number line is shown from 2 to 6 with an open circle on the point 4. The number line to the right of 4 is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_11.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00075">Try again. Revisit activities 2.9.2 and 2.9.3</para>
            <para id="para-00076">The correct answer is
                <media alt="A number line is shown from 2 to 6 with an open circle on the point 4. The number line to the right of 4 is shaded.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_12.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00077"> Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> The graph will have an open circle at 4, since the solution
              can not be equal to 4, with the arrow pointing to infinity to the right because the
              solution is greater than 4. The graph will have an open circle at 4, since the
              solution can not be equal to 4, with the arrow pointing to infinity to the right
              because the solution is greater than 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="cbd8f0f5-868b-4eb0-907d-8d32d19e0c12" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00078">Which number line represents the solution to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
            <para id="para-00079">
              
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_13.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00080">
              
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_14.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00081">
              
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_15.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00082">
              
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_16.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
           </para>
            <para id="para-00083">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00084">A.</para>
            <para id="para-00085">B.</para>
            <para id="para-00086">C.</para>
            <para id="para-00087">D.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00088">Correct! 
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_17.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00089">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.5</para>
            <para id="para-00090">The correct answer is
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_15_18.jpg"/>
                </media>
             </para>
            <para id="para-00091"> Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> The graph will have
              an open circle at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, since the solution can not be equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, with the arrow pointing to infinity to the left because the solution is
              less than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>. The graph will have an open circle at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>,
              since the solution can not be equal to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, with the arrow pointing to
              infinity to the left because the solution is less than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_865a1d9b-7090-4ea4-97a2-8957c4880e3f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00092">Find the solution set to this inequality by solving the related equation:
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00093">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00094"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&lt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00095"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00096"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00097"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00098">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00099">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.5</para>
            <para id="para-00100">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00101"> Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_74ac8378-e680-406b-8f15-d884098ae579" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00102">Here is an inequality: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>. What value of
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> will produce equality (or make the two sides equal)?</para>
            <para id="para-00103"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> = ____</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00104">Correct! 2</para>
            <para id="para-00105">Try again. Revisit activity 2.9.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00106">The correct answer is 2.</para>
            <para id="para-00107"> Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00108"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3pt" columnspacing="0em 2em"><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>28</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>28</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>28</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> The solution 2 will produce equality. It will
              make both sides equal. The solution 2 will produce equality. It will make both sides
              equal.</para>
            <para id="para-00109"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
              3 3</para>
            <para id="para-00110"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> 3 3</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
